# DevOps Cloud Platform

A production-style DevOps portfolio project demonstrating an end-to-end **CI/CD pipeline, containerization, Kubernetes deployment, HTTPS ingress, and monitoring**.

The project uses **Jenkins** to automatically test, build, tag, push, and deploy Docker images to **Kubernetes on Minikube**.

---

## 🚀 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how a modern DevOps workflow can automate application delivery from source code to a Kubernetes cluster.

### The pipeline

```text
Developer
    │
    ▼
 GitHub
    │
    ▼
 Jenkins
    │
    ├── Run Backend Tests
    │
    ├── Build Docker Images
    │
    ├── Generate Git SHA Image Tag
    │
    └── Push Images to Docker Hub
            │
            ▼
    Windows Minikube Agent
            │
            ▼
       Kubernetes
       ┌───────────────┐
       │   Ingress     │
       │ HTTPS / TLS   │
       └───────┬───────┘
               │
        ┌──────┴──────┐
        ▼             ▼
    Frontend        Backend
    2 replicas      2 replicas
        │             │
        └──────┬──────┘
               ▼
          Monitoring
       Prometheus + Grafana
```

---

## 🎯 Project Goals

The main objective was to build a realistic DevOps platform rather than a simple Dockerized application.

The project demonstrates:

- Git-based source control
- Automated CI/CD with Jenkins
- Automated backend testing
- Docker image creation
- Immutable SHA-based image tagging
- Docker Hub image publishing
- Kubernetes deployments
- Kubernetes Services
- Multiple application replicas
- Readiness and liveness probes
- Kubernetes service discovery
- NGINX Ingress
- HTTPS/TLS
- Automated Kubernetes deployments
- Prometheus monitoring
- Grafana visualization
- Jenkins deployment through a dedicated Windows/Minikube agent

